      "math_academy_id": "e-4790",
      "problem": "Find $\\mathbf{x},$ if $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14244365/assets/08ea17d62ec49da73a1144300483a1d6375d79465cb95e7871c89c556d8d0289.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $\\mathbf{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
